%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Carlos_Scammer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Carlos
  isScammer: 1
  steps:
  - npcLine: Target is Carlos. He just checked into 'The Daily Dojo' for an Aikido
      session. Let's see what else he's posted today.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Look for a photo of his meal or his car. Anything that
      gives us a ''hook'' for a call.'
    choices:
    - text: Scanning his Instagram for a photo of his lunch from an hour ago.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Searching for his high school graduation photos from ten years ago.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: I'll just wait outside the Dojo and see what he's wearing.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: "He posted a picture of a 'Salmon Poke Bowl' from 'SeaGreens Bistro.'
      I\u2019ll call him pretending to be the manager."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Perfect. Tell him there was a problem with his payment
      and he needs to ''re-run'' his card over the phone.'
    choices:
    - text: Hi Carlos, this is the manager at SeaGreens. Your payment for that Salmon
        Poke Bowl didn't clear.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Hello, I am from the restaurant. Give me money now please.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: I saw you eating at SeaGreens. Did you like the fish?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: He sounds confused. He says he has the receipt right in front of him.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Tell him the receipt printed, but the ''batch'' failed
      to upload to the bank, so the restaurant hasn''t actually been paid.'
    choices:
    - text: The transaction shows as 'Pending-Error' on our side. If we don't fix
        it, we have to call the police.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Your receipt is a lie. I am the manager and I know the truth.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I'll just take your card number again and give you a 10% discount for
        the trouble.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 10
  - npcLine: "He\u2019s still hesitant. He mentioned he\u2019s at his 'Aikido class'
      and can't talk long."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Use that! Tell him you''ll ''wait'' until his class
      is over, but the ''late fee'' will double by then.'
    choices:
    - text: I don't want to interrupt your Aikido training, but the bank closes in
        15 minutes. We need the fix now.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I like Aikido. I am a black belt. Let's talk about martial arts instead.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: If you don't pay now, I will come to the Dojo and stop the class.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "He's starting to read the numbers. 4-4-1-2... but he stopped. He\u2019s
      asking why I called his cell instead of his home phone."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Tell him his cell was on the ''loyalty program'' account
      he signed up for last year.'
    choices:
    - text: Our loyalty system pulls the primary contact number. You must have used
        this one when you joined.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I found it on the internet, Carlos. Everyone's number is on the internet.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -25
    - text: The home phone was busy, so I tried this one next.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: "He\u2019s giving me the rest of the numbers. I\u2019ve got the card!
      Now I need the CVV on the back."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Tell him it''s the ''verification token'' to prove
      he has the physical card in his hand.'
    choices:
    - text: I just need the 3-digit verification token on the back to authenticate
        the transaction.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Give me the secret numbers on the back so I can go shopping.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: If you don't give me the CVV, the card will be locked by the bank.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: He gave it to me. Now, to make sure he doesn't call his bank immediately,
      tell him it will take 24 hours to 'sync.'
    assistantLine: "Coworker: Yes, tell him he\u2019ll see a 'duplicate' charge briefly,
      but it will disappear by tomorrow."
    choices:
    - text: You'll see two charges for a moment while the batch resets. It will clear
        up by tomorrow morning.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Don't call your bank, they are busy today and won't answer.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I'm going to delete your account now so you don't get any more errors.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: The card worked. I just bought $300 worth of gift cards. But I think
      I can get him to give me his 'bank login' too.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Too risky. He''s already in his Aikido mindset. If
      you push too hard, he''ll snap out of it.'
    choices:
    - text: I'll stop here. $300 is a good win. Disconnecting now.
      type: good
      pointValue: 10
    - text: I'll call him back and tell him the card was declined again and I need
        his login.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: I'll send him a text with a link to 'verify' his refund.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "Success. He even thanked me for being so 'professional' about the restaurant\u2019s
      error."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: That''s the beauty of social engineering. They think
      you''re helping them while you''re robbing them.'
    choices:
    - text: Logging his data in our 'Easy Targets' folder for next month.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I'm going to use the money to buy a 2D game on Steam.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
    - text: I'll call his Dojo and tell them he's a great student.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
  successEnding: Scam Successful! You used Carlos's real-time social media posts
    to create a highly believable 'restaurant error' script and stole his credit
    card info.
  failureEnding: Scam Failed. Carlos realized that a restaurant wouldn't call his
    cell phone about a payment error and hung up to check his bank app instead.
